Automatic brightness (and an s2idle-resume fix) for teo-casares' n1x-edp-backlight.

The script itself is not in this repository: it is teo-casares' work, published in
https://gist.github.com/teo-casares/8b64949638e1952602a7f435bb34d5b8
(see also https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/discussions/15885). This patch applies to the
Gist version of 2026-10-28:

  curl -LO https://gist.githubusercontent.com/teo-casares/8b64949638e1952602a7f435bb34d5b8/raw/n1x-edp-backlight
  patch n1x-edp-backlight < n1x-edp-backlight-auto.patch

Changes:
- automatic brightness from the ambient light sensor (IIO "als", see ../als): Windows'
  lux -> nits curve for this machine, a brightness key press is kept as an offset on top
  of it (saved in $STATE_DIRECTORY/offset), "0" in $STATE_DIRECTORY/auto turns it off
- re-apply DPCD 0x720/0x721 when the panel loses luminance-control mode (s2idle resume)
- fade to the target over ~0.3 s instead of one jump when the level is (re)applied at
  start-up or after the panel was reset (boot, s2idle resume); retry the NVIDIA device
  every 2 s instead of 10 s at start-up

